# Ocentra Parent Logging and Redaction Rules

Logs are product data boundaries. This project may eventually observe child-device activity, so logging must be conservative from the start.

## Structured Logs Only

- Use `@ocentra-parent/logging-domain` for TypeScript log shapes.
- Use `crates/agent-protocol` constants and structs for Rust log snapshots.
- Do not add raw console logging in app/runtime code.
- Do not invent log fields at call sites.

## Redaction First

Never log:

- child names
- account secrets
- auth tokens
- raw screenshots
- raw URLs from browsing activity
- full process command lines
- keystrokes
- clipboard content
- message contents

If a field might later contain sensitive activity, store a stable category, status, or redacted summary instead.

## Diagnostics

Dev diagnostics must be useful without leaking private data:

- service version
- platform
- mode
- feature enabled flags
- correlation ids
- schema versions
- event types

Add tests when adding log shapes or redaction behavior.

